    {
      "path": ".claude/scripts/with-browser-lock.sh",
      "content": "Stale-lock recovery can remove a new owner's live lock. Two waiters can both read the dead PID; waiter A moves the stale directory and acquires a new lock, then waiter B executes this move against A's new directory. Both can subsequently run commands, and A's unconditional release can also delete B's lock. Atomic rename alone does not make the preceding ownership check atomic. Serialize stale recovery with acquisition (or use an OS-managed lock) so a waiter cannot reclaim a replacement lock.",
      "existing_code": "    stale=\"$lock.stale.$$\"\n    mv \"$lock\" \"$stale\" 2\u003e/dev/null \u0026\u0026 rm -rf \"$stale\"",
      "start_line": 49,
      "end_line": 50,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": ".claude/scripts/with-browser-lock.sh",
      "content": "This terminates only the immediate child, but full-suite.sh invokes command chains through bash/npm/npx. Terminating that shell or runner can leave its descendants running; once the immediate child exits, this wrapper removes the lock and another browser run can start against still-active servers or builds. Run the command in an isolated process group and terminate/wait for the group before releasing the lock.",
      "existing_code": "  [[ -n \"$child\" ]] \u0026\u0026 kill -TERM \"$child\" 2\u003e/dev/null",
      "start_line": 31,
      "end_line": 31,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": ".claude/scripts/run-complete.sh",
      "content": "Missing browser evidence now makes any run look like an intentional lane run. For example, a task/full run whose unit, integration and checks stages finished but whose browser stage was never started will now return 'run complete', whereas previously it reported missing browser evidence. Since this script gates cumulative-run reporting, require an explicit lane tier argument or persisted tier marker rather than inferring permission to omit browser tests from their absence.",
      "existing_code": "elif [[ ! -f \"$dir/$label-browser.txt\" ]]; then\n  stages=(unit integration checks) # lane tier (decision 111): no browser file at all",
      "start_line": 15,
      "end_line": 16,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": ".claude/scripts/lane-setup.sh",
      "content": "This strips from the first `.claude/worktrees/` component, not the one containing the lane. If the deliverable is itself a Claude worktree, e.g. `/repo/.claude/worktrees/deliverable/.claude/worktrees/lane`, `source_root` becomes `/repo` instead of the deliverable root. Setup then copies another checkout's dependencies, release artifacts and environment (or fails if that checkout is not installed). Strip the shortest matching suffix (`${root%/.claude/worktrees/*}`) so nested lane worktrees use their immediate deliverable worktree.",
      "suggestion_code": "source_root=${root%/.claude/worktrees/*}",
      "existing_code": "source_root=${root%%/.claude/worktrees/*}",
      "start_line": 20,
      "end_line": 20,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
